<Layout title="About" description="About Anime Story Films — original fiction film stories, told as a video clip and a full written story.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    <strong>Anime Story Films</strong> is a blog of original fiction film
    stories. Every film here is told twice: first as a short cinematic
    video clip — the trailer — and then in full, in writing, episode by
    episode. The video is the hook. The writing is the film.
  </p>
  <p>
    All of our stories are original. No fan films, no borrowed characters,
    no copyrighted worlds — just new stories, made to be watched and read.
  </p>

  <h2>The format</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Watch</strong> the clip at the top of each episode.</li>
    <li><strong>Read</strong> the full story underneath it.</li>
    <li><strong>Continue</strong> — every episode ends on a cliffhanger.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Our first film: Ember Blade</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Ember Blade</strong> is our first film: a retro 1990s anime
    action story set in feudal Japan. Ryu, 19, the last fire-sword
    swordsman, buried his katana three years ago and swore never to use
    its fire again — until the man who burned his village came back.
  </p>
  <p>
    Episode 1, “The Village That Burned Twice,” is out now. New episodes
    are published as the story is finished, scene by scene.
  </p>
